\section{The client}

The client is shaped like Unpaywall's: an HTTP session, a per-DOI cache
in its own [[europepmc.pkl]] (so [[scholar cache info]] and [[scholar
cache clear --provider europepmc]] cover it), and a limiter declared as
[[LIMITS]], which [[scholar providers limits]] lists
(\cref{sec:ratelimit-registry}).
It keeps the outcome of its last lookup the way the providers' DOI
lookups do (\cref{sec:lookup-outcome}): [[last_lookup_error]] when the
lookup failed, [[last_lookup_declined]] when there was nothing it could
ask.

<<the europe pmc client>>=
class EuropePMCClient:
    """Looks up abstracts for DOIs via Europe PMC's RESTful search."""

    name = "europepmc"
    LIMITS = Limits(per_second=EUROPEPMC_REQUESTS_PER_SECOND)

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self._cache: dict = load_cache(self.name)
        register_cache(self.name, self._cache)
        self._limiter = limiter_for(self)
        self._session = self._create_session()
        self.last_lookup_error: str | None = None
        self.last_lookup_declined: str | None = None

    <<europe pmc client methods>>
<<constants>>=
EUROPEPMC_SEARCH_URL = (
    "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search"
)
EUROPEPMC_TIMEOUT = 30
EUROPEPMC_REQUESTS_PER_SECOND = 5.0  # scholar's choice; see the prose
@

The session is a [[ScholarSession]] (\cref{ch:network}), with
scholar's User-Agent and the configured route, and the back-off the
other clients use, so a transient 5xx is retried before it counts as a
failure.

<<europe pmc client methods>>=
def _create_session(self) -> requests.Session:
    """Create a session with exponential back-off retry logic."""
    retry = Retry(
        total=3,
        backoff_factor=1,  # 1s, 2s, 4s delays
        status_forcelist=[429, 500, 502, 503, 504],
        allowed_methods=["GET"],
    )
    return network.new_session(retry)
@

\subsection{Looking an abstract up}

The lookup returns the abstract, or [[None]] for every other outcome,
and leaves in the attributes which outcome it was.
An answer---one record with an abstract, records without one, or no
record---is cached, the absence of an abstract as [[None]], so a DOI
Europe PMC does not hold is not asked again on the next run.
A failure is not cached, and [[last_lookup_error]] holds the reason in
the words of [[network.request_failure_reason]]
(\cref{sec:request-failure-reason}).
An answer that is JSON but has no result list is a failure too: we
cannot tell it from an answer, so it must not be cached as one.

A DOI holding a double quote cannot be put inside the speech marks of a
phrase, and the OpenAPI description says nothing about escaping one; we
decline such a DOI instead of sending a query whose meaning we do not
know.

Several results are asked for ([[EUROPEPMC_PAGE_SIZE]]) because we take
the first whose DOI is ours and which has an abstract, and the
documentation does not promise that a DOI matches one record only.

<<constants>>=
EUROPEPMC_PAGE_SIZE = 5
<<europe pmc client methods>>=
def fetch_abstract(self, doi: str | None) -> str | None:
    """Return the abstract Europe PMC holds for `doi`, or None.

    None when there is no DOI, Europe PMC holds no record with an
    abstract for it, the DOI cannot be asked for, or the lookup
    failed; the last two set `last_lookup_declined` and
    `last_lookup_error`.
    """
    self.last_lookup_error = None
    self.last_lookup_declined = None
    if not doi:
        return None
    if '"' in doi:
        self.last_lookup_declined = EUROPEPMC_UNQUOTABLE_DOI
        return None
    key = ("abstract", doi)
    if key in self._cache:
        logger.debug("europepmc: cache hit for DOI %s", doi)
        return self._cache[key]
    try:
        self._limiter.acquire()
        response = self._session.get(
            EUROPEPMC_SEARCH_URL,
            params={
                "query": f'DOI:"{doi}"',
                "resultType": "core",
                "format": "json",
                "pageSize": EUROPEPMC_PAGE_SIZE,
            },
            timeout=EUROPEPMC_TIMEOUT,
        )
        self._limiter.record_response(response)
        response.raise_for_status()
        abstract = abstract_for_doi(doi, response.json())
    except RateLimited as e:
        self.last_lookup_error = e.reason
        return None
    except Exception as e:
        logger.warning(
            "europepmc: lookup failed for %s: %s",
            doi, network.redact_secrets(e),
        )
        self.last_lookup_error = network.request_failure_reason(e)
        return None
    self._cache[key] = abstract
    return abstract
<<constants>>=
EUROPEPMC_UNQUOTABLE_DOI = "the DOI holds a double quote"
@

Reading the answer is a function of its own, so the tests can feed it
the recorded bodies directly.
The abstract is returned as the service sent it: the recorded one is
plain text, and what markup other records may carry is not documented
in what we could read.
Whatever entities or inline tags arrive are removed by
[[clean_metadata_text]] at the end of [[enrich_paper]], as for every
provider (\cref{sec:clean-provider-text}).

<<module-level europe pmc interface>>=
def abstract_for_doi(doi: str, answer: dict) -> str | None:
    """Return the abstract of the first result under `doi` in `answer`.

    `answer` is a decoded search response. Raises `ValueError` when it
    has no result list, since that cannot be told from "no record".
    """
    try:
        results = answer["resultList"]["result"]
    except (KeyError, TypeError):
        raise ValueError("answer without a result list") from None
    wanted = doi.casefold()
    for record in results or []:
        text = record.get("abstractText")
        if (
            str(record.get("doi") or "").casefold() == wanted
            and isinstance(text, str)
            and text.strip()
        ):
            return text.strip()
    return None
@

Enrichment asks for a paper ([[get_paper_by_doi]],
\cref{enrich-module}); ours holds the DOI and the abstract only, with
Europe PMC as its source, as Crossref's does
(\cref{sec:crossref-abstract}).

<<europe pmc client methods>>=
def get_paper_by_doi(self, doi: str | None) -> Paper | None:
    """Return a paper holding only `doi` and its Europe PMC abstract."""
    abstract = self.fetch_abstract(doi)
    if not abstract:
        return None
    return Paper(
        title="", authors=[], doi=doi, abstract=abstract,
        sources=[self.name],
    )
@

\section{The module-level interface}

One client is built at import, so its cache, session and limiter are
shared by the whole process; enrichment asks that client.

<<module-level europe pmc interface>>=
_client = EuropePMCClient()


def fetch_abstract(doi: str | None) -> str | None:
    """Look up the abstract of a DOI (see EuropePMCClient)."""
    return _client.fetch_abstract(doi)


def last_lookup_error() -> str | None:
    """Why the shared client's last lookup failed; None if it did not."""
    return _client.last_lookup_error


def enrichment_source() -> EuropePMCClient:
    """The shared client, as an abstract source for `scholar.enrich`."""
    return _client
@

\section{Tests}

The tests replay the two recorded answers, trimmed to what the code
reads (the result list, each result's [[doi]] and [[abstractText]],
plus identifiers and title for the reader); the abstract is cut to its
first two sentences.
They check the outcomes the lookup promises: the abstract of the
matching record, an answer without a record that is cached, a failure
that is not, a declined DOI that sends nothing, and the request we send.

<<test functions>>=
# Recorded 2026-11-20 from
# https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search
#   ?query=DOI:"10.7717/peerj.4375"&resultType=core&format=json&pageSize=5
# trimmed; the abstract (licence "cc by") cut to two sentences.
RECORDED_HIT = {
    "version": "6.9",
    "hitCount": 1,
    "resultList": {"result": [{
        "id": "29456894",
        "source": "MED",
        "pmid": "29456894",
        "pmcid": "PMC5815332",
        "doi": "10.7717/peerj.4375",
        "title": (
            "The state of OA: a large-scale analysis of the prevalence "
            "and impact of Open Access articles."
        ),
        "abstractText": (
            "Despite growing interest in Open Access (OA) to scholarly "
            "literature, there is an unmet need for large-scale, "
            "up-to-date, and reproducible studies assessing the "
            "prevalence and characteristics of OA. We address this need "
            "using oaDOI, an open online service that determines OA "
            "status for 67 million articles."
        ),
    }]},
}
# Recorded 2026-11-20, the same query for DOI:"10.1109/CVPR.2016.90".
RECORDED_NO_HIT = {
    "version": "6.9",
    "hitCount": 0,
    "request": {
        "queryString": 'DOI:"10.1109/CVPR.2016.90"', "resultType": "core",
        "cursorMark": "*", "pageSize": 5, "sort": "", "synonym": False,
    },
    "resultList": {"result": []},
}


class TestEuropePMCAbstract:
    """The abstract lookup and its outcomes (#260)."""

    DOI = "10.7717/peerj.4375"

    def _replay(self, data=RECORDED_HIT, status=200):
        return patch.object(
            _client._session, "get",
            return_value=_mock_response(status, data),
        )

    def test_recorded_hit_gives_the_abstract(self):
        with self._replay():
            paper = _client.get_paper_by_doi(self.DOI)
        assert paper.abstract.startswith("Despite growing interest")
        assert paper.abstract.endswith("for 67 million articles.")
        assert paper.sources == ["europepmc"]
        assert _client.last_lookup_error is None

    def test_request_asks_for_the_doi_with_core_results(self):
        with self._replay() as get:
            fetch_abstract(self.DOI)
        url = get.call_args.args[0]
        params = get.call_args.kwargs["params"]
        assert url == EUROPEPMC_SEARCH_URL
        assert params["query"] == 'DOI:"10.7717/peerj.4375"'
        assert params["resultType"] == "core"
        assert params["format"] == "json"
        assert "email" not in params

    def test_doi_matches_regardless_of_case(self):
        with self._replay():
            assert fetch_abstract("10.7717/PEERJ.4375")

    def test_no_record_is_a_cached_answer(self):
        with self._replay(RECORDED_NO_HIT) as get:
            assert fetch_abstract("10.1109/CVPR.2016.90") is None
            assert last_lookup_error() is None
            assert fetch_abstract("10.1109/CVPR.2016.90") is None
        assert get.call_count == 1

    def test_result_under_another_doi_is_not_taken(self):
        with self._replay():
            assert fetch_abstract("10.1/other") is None

    def test_answer_is_cached(self):
        with self._replay() as get:
            fetch_abstract(self.DOI)
            fetch_abstract(self.DOI)
        assert get.call_count == 1

    @pytest.mark.parametrize("failure, reason", [
        (requests.exceptions.ConnectionError("x"),
         "connection failed (ConnectionError)"),
        (requests.exceptions.RetryError("x"), network.RETRIES_SPENT),
    ])
    def test_failure_is_neither_cached_nor_silent(self, failure, reason):
        with patch.object(_client._session, "get", side_effect=failure):
            assert fetch_abstract(self.DOI) is None
        assert last_lookup_error() == reason
        assert ("abstract", self.DOI) not in _client._cache
        with self._replay() as get:
            assert fetch_abstract(self.DOI)
        assert get.call_count == 1

    def test_server_error_is_a_failure(self):
        with self._replay({}, status=500):
            assert fetch_abstract(self.DOI) is None
        assert last_lookup_error() == "HTTP 500"
        assert ("abstract", self.DOI) not in _client._cache

    def test_answer_without_result_list_is_a_failure(self):
        with self._replay({"hitCount": 1}):
            assert fetch_abstract(self.DOI) is None
        assert last_lookup_error() == "answer without a result list"
        assert ("abstract", self.DOI) not in _client._cache

    def test_doi_with_a_quote_is_declined_without_a_request(self):
        with self._replay() as get:
            assert fetch_abstract('10.1/a"b') is None
        get.assert_not_called()
        assert _client.last_lookup_declined == EUROPEPMC_UNQUOTABLE_DOI
        assert _client.last_lookup_error is None
